{"segs": ["PA_ja_206:0.4", "PA_ja_206:1.1"], "en": "6. The Kuruṅga Deer Jātaka “Come now, tortoise,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_206:1.2"], "en": "cut through this snare made of rope with your tusks!”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_206:1.3", "PA_ja_206:1.4"], "en": "\"I shall act in such a way that the hunter will not come here.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_206:2.1"], "en": "The tortoise entered the water.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_206:2.2"], "en": "The kuruṅga deer entered the forest;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_206:2.3"], "en": "with a hundred feathers,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_206:2.4"], "en": "he carried his young ones far away from the treetop.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_206:3.1"], "en": "The Sixth Jātaka: The Kuruṅga Deer.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
